{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group D of the 1986 FIFA World Cup''' was one of the groups of nations competing at the [[1986 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's first round of matches began on 1 June and its last matches were played on 12 June. Most matches were played at the [[Estadio Jalisco]] and the [[Estadio Tres de Marzo]] in [[Guadalajara]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/86full.html |title=World Cup 1986 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Undefeated [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], with three clean slate shutouts, topped the group; [[Spain national football team|Spain]] finished second. Both teams advanced to the second round. [[Northern Ireland national football team|Northern Ireland]] and [[Algeria national football team|Algeria]] were the other two teams in the group.

